  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DNA Sample Collection Support to Dutch Immigration and Naturalisation Service for Family Reunification (2022-2023)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Within the scope of this pilot project, IOM will coordinate the DNA collection process according to the established standard operating procedures, in collaboration with the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Dutch Immigration and Naturalisation Service (IND). As the backlogs and prognoses of the IND are uncertain for 2021 and likely to fluctuate, IOM is flexible in assessing possibilities in requests from countries other than Sudan, Greece, Lebanon and Turkey and therefore includes a caseload based on dossiers. In addition, IOM will facilitate identification interviews for applicants in Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
